Statement: "Because the page exports revalidate = 300, the catalog HTML is still rendered at most once every 5 minutes and served from the cache in between."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The build output marks /courses as ƒ, rendered on demand: a route is rendered for each request as soon as anything in its tree (the page or any layout above it) reads a request-time API such as cookies(), headers() or searchParams. The root layout reads cookies() for the theme, so every route below it, the catalog included, is rendered per request and revalidate = 300 cannot cache the HTML (depending on your Next.js version it may still affect how the data fetches inside are cached, but not the page). The misconception is that revalidate is a setting of the page alone; the whole tree decides, and one cookie read in a shared layout outranks it. The fix is to stop reading the cookie on the server, then confirm in the build output that the route is no longer ƒ.', 1, 5
