// components/EnrollButton.tsx starts with "use client"

Error during rendering:
Error: Functions cannot be passed directly to Client Components unless you explicitly expose it by marking it with "use server". Or maybe you meant to call this function rather than return it.
  <... courseId="c_42" onEnrolled={function onEnrolled}>

Statement: "Moving the onEnrolled logic into EnrollButton and passing only courseId (a string) from the page removes this error."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. Props that go from a server component to a client component are serialized by React and sent with the page; a string serializes, an ordinary function does not, because its code and closure live on the server. When the click handling lives inside EnrollButton, the function is created in the browser and never crosses the boundary. A Server Function (marked "use server") is the exception: it crosses as a reference the client can call. The misconception is that a prop is just a JavaScript value passed in memory; across this boundary it is data on the wire, so it must be data (strings, numbers, plain objects, arrays, Dates, JSX) and not behaviour.', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nrc_121') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
