The web server runs Node in the UTC time zone with the default en-US locale.
Error tracker, last 7 days: 2,340 hydration errors; browser locale vi-VN 97%, en-US 3%.
Dev overlay for a vi-VN browser in Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh:
+ 149.000 VND          (client)
- 149,000 VND          (server)
+ Enrolled 26/10/2026  (client)
- Enrolled 10/25/2026  (server)

Statement: "Setting TZ=Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh on the web server fixes the hydration errors for Vietnamese learners."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The time zone explains only part of the date (25 vs 26 October for a timestamp late in the UTC evening). Both lines also differ in format: the server formats with its default locale en-US (149,000 and month/day/year) and the browser with vi-VN (149.000 and day/month/year), and TZ does not change the locale. A server-wide time zone would also be wrong for every learner outside Vietnam. The fix is to stop relying on defaults: format with an explicit locale and time zone, preferably once on the server, and pass the string to the client component. The misconception is that a mismatch has a single cause; read every line of the diff before choosing a fix.', 1, 5
