Statement: "Because the course list is public data, this key is safe; leaving level and locale out of it only lowers the hit rate."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The key leaves out inputs that change the result: level and locale are passed to db.listCourses, so the request for advanced courses at 09:14:05 is answered with the beginner list stored at 09:14:02. That is a correctness bug, not a hit-rate problem. "Public" only says the result does not depend on who asks; it still depends on every other input. The misconception mixes up the two failures of a key: a missing input gives wrong answers, an extra input (such as utm_source or the user id on public data) lowers the hit rate.', 1, 5
