Statement: "For up to 300 seconds the CDN can serve the Vietnamese titles to a browser that sent Accept-Language: en, because the language changes the result but is neither in the URL nor named in a Vary header."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. A shared cache builds its key from the URL plus the request headers listed in Vary. Here the URL is the same for both languages and there is no Vary, so the first response stored (Vietnamese, if a Vietnamese browser asked first) is served to everyone for up to s-maxage=300 seconds. The fix is to make the locale part of the URL (/vi/api/courses) or to send Vary: Accept-Language and check your CDN supports it. The misconception is that the server cache key is the only key: every cache on the way builds its own.', 2, 5
