INSERT INTO challenge.challenges (public_id, course_id, module_id, lesson_id, name, title, description, status, difficulty, type, points, is_published, is_deleted)
VALUES ('chal_coding_nrc_212', (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'nextjs-rendering-caching'), (SELECT id FROM course.module WHERE course_id = (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'nextjs-rendering-caching') AND order_index = 2 AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), (SELECT id FROM course.lesson WHERE content_source = 'lesson-nrc-2-1' AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), 'safe-cache-keys', 'Build safe cache keys', 'Every data request of app.codedev.test goes through cachePolicy(request), which returns the key of the server data cache (null = do not cache) and the Cache-Control header of the response. The old code cached the course list under "courses:<category>": advanced filters got the beginner list, Vietnamese learners got English titles and every newsletter link created a new entry. RESOURCES in the starter lists each resource with its classification (public, per-user, private-no-store), its route params, the query params the API understands with their defaults, whether it is localized, and sMaxAge.

Rules, in this order. (1) A resource that is not an own key of RESOURCES (for example "courses" or "toString") -> throw Error("unknown resource: <name>"). A route param of the resource that is missing or empty after trimming -> throw Error("missing param: <name>") for the first such param in RESOURCES order; extra params are ignored. Per-user or private-no-store data with a userId that is missing, null or empty after trimming -> throw Error("personal data needs a signed-in user").

(2) private-no-store -> { key: null, cacheControl: "private, no-store" }.

(3) The key is the resource name, then "/" + each route param value (trimmed) in RESOURCES order, then, only if the resource has query params, "?" + every known query param in alphabetical order as name=value joined by "&", then "|locale=<locale>" if the resource is localized, then "|user=<userId>" (trimmed) if it is per-user. A query value is the first one if the param is repeated (an array), trimmed and lower-cased; missing or empty means the default. Unknown query params are dropped. The locale is trimmed, lower-cased and cut at the first "-" ("vi-VN" -> "vi"); a language not in LOCALES, or no locale, becomes "en". Every param value, query value and user id put in the key goes through encodeURIComponent. Public keys never contain the user, even when one is signed in; non-localized keys never contain the locale.

(4) Cache-Control: public -> "public, max-age=0, s-maxage=<sMaxAge>", per-user -> "private, no-cache".

Input: { "requests": [{ resource, params?, query?, locale?, userId? }, ...] }. The runner prints "<key> | <cacheControl>" per request ("(not cached)" for a null key) or "error: <message>", then "<n> requests, <m> cache entries" (distinct keys).', 'open', 'medium'::difficulty_question, 'mini_coding', 30, true, false)
