Statement: "Each of the two requests carried a different session cookie, so a shared cache that follows the HTTP caching rules keeps a separate copy per cookie: the CDN cannot be the layer that mixed the two learners."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. A shared cache keys a stored response by the request URL, plus the request headers the response names in Vary. Cookies are not part of the key unless the response says Vary: Cookie, and this one does not. The header public, s-maxage=60 explicitly tells shared caches they may store the response and reuse it for 60 seconds, for any request to /api/dashboard. So the CDN did exactly what it was told, and B shows it serving one stored copy to two cookies. The misconception is that a cache somehow "knows" a response is personal because the request was authenticated; it only knows what the URL, Vary and Cache-Control say.', 2, 5
