Statement: "This is a stale page after the instructor''s 08:55 edit: the dashboard shows data from before the edit, and calling revalidatePath(\"/dashboard\") after every lesson completion would fix it."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Stale means the right learner''s data, but old. A shows another learner''s data (Minh''s name, lessons and streak shown to Lan), which is a leak, not staleness. D also puts the start at Monday 17:40, before the 08:55 edit, and the edit changed a course title, not anyone''s progress. Revalidating the dashboard path would only empty the shared entry so that the next learner refills it: the leak would rotate faster, not stop. The question to ask first is whose data it is; a shorter TTL or more revalidation never fixes a key that leaves out the user.', 5, 5
