Proposed fix: the data cache key becomes `dashboard:${userId}` (userId read from the session outside the cached function), /api/dashboard is sent with Cache-Control: private, no-cache, /api/courses keeps public, max-age=0, s-maxage=300, and /api/dashboard is purged at the CDN after the deploy.

Statement: "A test that requests the dashboard as Lan and then as Minh through a simulated CDN, once with the CDN in front and once bypassed, and asserts each learner gets their own data, fails on the release code and passes with this fix."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. On the release code both modes fail: with the CDN in front, Minh gets Lan''s stored response (public, same URL); with the CDN bypassed, the data cache returns Lan''s entry under "dashboard". With the fix, the key contains the user, so the data cache keeps one entry per learner (the expensive query is still cached for 60 seconds), and private keeps every shared cache from storing the response, while the public course list is still shared. Testing both modes matters because each half-fix passes one of them. The purge is needed because entries stored under the old public header live until they expire.', 6, 5
