VALUES ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_nrc_332'), 1, 'For each value on the page, ask: would it be the same if another person sent this request? Only the values where the answer is yes may go through deps.sharedCache; everything else is loaded for this request and forgotten.'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_nrc_332'), 2, 'Look at what you store under course:<id>: the course and the time you stored it, nothing derived from the user. Then look at the order of the personal loads: anonymous visitors stop before any of them, and an enrolled learner stops before the coupon. The freshness check uses < at the boundary, so an entry stored at 0 with ttl 300 is reloaded at 300.'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_nrc_332'), 3, 'A similar split on the lesson page, with ttl 60: the lesson body is public and cached as lesson:<id>; a learner''s notes are personal. Requests at 0 (Lan), 30 (anonymous) and 60 (Binh) for lesson 9 give the loads [public:9 notes:lan:9], [] and [public:9 notes:binh:9], and the shared cache ends with the single key lesson:9: Binh never sees Lan''s notes and the body was loaded once per minute.');
