Statement: "A request for /courses/sql-joins-in-practice is rendered on demand when it first arrives instead of answering 404, because generateStaticParams only decides which pages are prerendered at build."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. With dynamicParams left at its default (true), a param value that generateStaticParams did not return is rendered when it is first requested, and for an otherwise static route the result is cached for later visitors. generateStaticParams is a list of pages to prepare ahead of time, not a list of pages that are allowed to exist. The page then loads the course, finds it and renders it; only a slug with no course reaches notFound(). The common misconception is that generateStaticParams works as a whitelist; that is only the case when dynamicParams is set to false.', 1, 5
