The day after the deploy, an instructor publishes the new course "rust-for-web-devs". No deploy follows.

Statement: "/courses/rust-for-web-devs will render on its first request and be cached for an hour, because its data fetch has revalidate: 3600 and a course tag."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. With dynamicParams = false, any slug that generateStaticParams did not return at build time answers 404, whatever the data fetch inside the page would do: the page never runs for that slug. The new course stays a 404 until the next build includes it in the list (and only if it is in the top 200). revalidate and tags control how long the data of pages that do render stays fresh; they do not add new pages to a closed list. The common misconception is that ISR settings on the fetch make new paths appear; that depends on dynamicParams. Rejecting junk slugs is better done with input validation and notFound() for slugs with no course.', 2, 5
