Server log for one request:
+0 ms    getModules        start
+152 ms  getModules        done
+152 ms  getReviewSummary  start
+290 ms  getReviewSummary  done

getReviewSummary(slug) reads only the slug; it uses nothing returned by getModules.

Statement: "Starting both loaders together with Promise.all([getModules(slug), getReviewSummary(slug)]) should bring this component''s data time to about 150 ms, the time of the slower loader."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The two loaders are independent: the second one needs only the slug, which is available before either starts. Awaiting them one after the other adds their times (152 + 138 = 290 ms); starting both and awaiting them together costs about the time of the slower one (about 152 ms). This is a waterfall inside a single component, and Suspense does not fix it: Suspense decides what can be sent early, not whether two requests run at the same time. Keep the sequence only when the second call needs a value from the first. The common misconception is that each await only blocks its own line; it blocks everything after it in that function.', 2, 5
