Statement: "Reading the cookie in the page explains why the catalog changed from prerendered to rendered on every request."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. cookies() reads per-request data, so Next.js can no longer prerender the page once for everyone: the route becomes dynamic, which is exactly what the legend shows (○ to ƒ). Comparing the route table of two builds finds this before any code reading, and the diff confirms it. A theme preference can be applied on the client or with a CSS media query so the catalog stays prerendered. The common misconception is that reading one small cookie only affects the component that uses it; in a page without other boundaries it changes how the whole route renders.', 3, 5
